The `catch_unwind` logic has been removed from `CatchTask::execute`. This removes panic safety from tasks wrapped with `.catch()`. While the comments indicate this might be temporary, removing this functionality makes `CatchTask` less useful and potentially misleading, as panics will now propagate and could crash a worker thread. It's recommended to restore the `std::panic::catch_unwind` logic for `std` builds to maintain panic boundary capabilities.

```rust
        #[cfg(feature = "std")]
        {
            match std::panic::catch_unwind(std::panic::AssertUnwindSafe(|| task.execute())) {
                Ok(result) => result,
                Err(_) => handler(),
            }
        }

        #[cfg(not(feature = "std"))]
        {
            // In no_std, we can't catch panics, so just execute normally
            task.execute()
        }
```

