_⚠️ Potential issue_

**Stop premature exit when an opening back-tick is unmatched.**

`tokenize_markdown` breaks out of the outer loop (`break;`) whenever it reaches the end of the string without finding a matching closing delimiter.  
If the unmatched span is **not the final fragment** of the line, every character that follows is silently discarded, so `wrap_preserving_code` can produce lines longer than the requested width and content is lost.

Tag the unmatched delimiter as a normal token and continue scanning instead of aborting:

```diff
@@ fn tokenize_markdown(text: &str) -> Vec<String> {
-            if end >= chars.len() {
-                tokens.push(chars[start..].iter().collect());
-                break;
+            if end >= chars.len() {
+                // Treat the opening delimeter as plain text and continue scanning.
+                tokens.push(chars[start..i].iter().collect());
+                continue;
             }
```

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
fn tokenize_markdown(text: &str) -> Vec<String> {
    let mut tokens = Vec::new();
    let chars: Vec<char> = text.chars().collect();
    let mut i = 0;
    while i < chars.len() {
        let c = chars[i];
        if c.is_whitespace() {
            let start = i;
            while i < chars.len() && chars[i].is_whitespace() {
                i += 1;
            }
            tokens.push(chars[start..i].iter().collect());
        } else if c == '`' {
            let start = i;
            let mut delim_len = 0;
            while i < chars.len() && chars[i] == '`' {
                i += 1;
                delim_len += 1;
            }
            let mut end = i;
            while end < chars.len() {
                if chars[end] == '`' {
                    let mut j = end;
                    let mut count = 0;
                    while j < chars.len() && chars[j] == '`' {
                        j += 1;
                        count += 1;
                    }
                    if count == delim_len {
                        end = j;
                        tokens.push(chars[start..end].iter().collect());
                        i = end;
                        break;
                    }
                }
                end += 1;
            }
            if end >= chars.len() {
                // Treat the opening delimeter as plain text and continue scanning.
                tokens.push(chars[start..i].iter().collect());
                continue;
            }
        } else {
            let start = i;
            while i < chars.len() && !chars[i].is_whitespace() && chars[i] != '`' {
                i += 1;
            }
            tokens.push(chars[start..i].iter().collect());
        }
    }
    tokens
}
```

</details>

